course: dictionary
lesson: 4532
title: Healthy: more than just not ill
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Healthy means well, strong and not ill. It can also describe things that help you stay well, like healthy food or a healthy habit.
explain: «Sadness is a normal feeling for everyone, and crying is a healthy way to let it out.» Here healthy means good for you. Crying helps, but holding feelings in does not make them go away.
explain: Healthy can also mean normal and good, as in a healthy plant, or large, as in «a healthy appetite». Look at the words around it to see which meaning fits.
fact: Healthy means well, strong and not ill.
fact: Healthy food and habits help you stay well, such as balanced meals, water, exercise and sleep.
fact: Healthy plants need light, water and nutrients.
fact: «Healthy» can mean large, as in «a healthy appetite».
fact: «Spinach is healthy, but it gives no sudden muscles»: muscles grow over months with exercise, food and rest.
exercise: «Spinach is healthy, but it gives no sudden muscles.» What does healthy mean here? | Sudden and fast | Very loud | *Good for your body, helping you stay well | Green and leafy
exercise: Which habit is healthy? | *Eating balanced meals and drinking water | Staying up all night | Eating only sweets | Never going outside
exercise: «Crying is a healthy way to let sadness out.» What does healthy mean in this sentence? | Angry and loud | *Good for you, helping you feel better | Full of energy from sugar | Ill and tired
test: What does healthy mean in «a healthy appetite»? | Small | Ill | Sleepy | *Large
test: Plants need light, water and what else to stay healthy? | Noise | Sweets | Snow | *Nutrients
exam: Which sentence uses healthy to mean well and not ill? | Mia ate a healthy snack at break | The gym sold healthy shakes | *After her cold, Maya is finally healthy again | Ben has a healthy appetite for pizza
